  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nA cold front will slowly push south across the area this \nafternoon into this evening. Scattered showers and stray \nthunderstorms remain possible across the southern part of the \narea, mainly along/south of US-30 in Ohio. Instability is meager\nand suppressed to the south of the area so severe weather is \nnot anticipated in any thunderstorms through this evening. Have \nincreased PoPs to slight chance/chance (20-40 percent) through \ntonight in the southern part of the area since a shortwave \ntrough may allow for some additional rain development. Dry \nconditions will develop by early Friday morning as high pressure\nbuilds into the area. Patchy to areas of fog (locally dense in\nspots) will develop across the area late tonight into early \nFriday morning given persistent low level moisture and light \nwinds\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \nAfter a brief break from both humidity and rain chances on \nFriday, shower and thunderstorm chances will return to the area \nSaturday as a warm front lifts through the region. The greatest \nprobability of showers and thunderstorms will be across southern\nand eastern areas during the day. The potential for gusty winds\nin thunderstorms is still there, but confidence is low due to \nlikelihood of daytime cloud cover and uncertainty with the \nplacement/timing of the best instability and forcing. Dew points\nwill once again reach the upper 60s and lower 70s on Saturday \nso it will be quite humid. Isolated showers can't be ruled out \nas a cold front attempts to cross the region on Sunday with dry\nweather favored on Monday as high pressure briefly builds in \nfrom the west. Another period of unsettled weather is likely as \na series of disturbances ripple across the region Tuesday \nthrough at least Wednesday, though there is still low confidence\nin the exact timing/placement of showers and thunderstorms and \nany resulting impacts/hazards.",
